msgstr "TCP 클라이언트 파일 전송 API"

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Client_APIs.rst:341
#: 15461ca186ed497083b901e65a3b33d1
msgid "External code can observe traffic without replacing the protocol loop:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Client_APIs.rst:351
#: 0d916f8d3eaf4336b5be87a5faf153a3
msgid ""
"``add_message_listener`` registers ``listener(sender_id, message)`` for "
"every inbound line, commands included, so a listener observes all inbound"
" traffic; a message another client forwarded here through the "
"``/send_msg_from`` envelope is reported as its payload. ``sender_id`` is "
"the author's ``\"ip:port\"`` — the forwarding client for such a forwarded"
" message, and it is ``None`` for a direct push from the server. "
"``add_file_listener`` registers ``listener(client_id, full_path, name, "
"size, command)`` and fires after a file sent by the server has been fully"
" written to disk. Both listeners run on a protocol thread, so they must "
"not block, and an exception inside a listener is logged and swallowed. "
"The ``remove_*`` counterparts unregister a listener and ignore unknown "
"ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Client_APIs.rst:364
#: 196be233dc00497a94ee87f9999a9897
msgid ""
"Received messages and events are also stored per sender socket in "
"``messages_dict`` / ``events_dict`` (each entry a ``[content, "
"timestamp]`` pair). When a store reaches ``max_dict_size`` (64 KiB) it is"
" flushed to ``messages_log.json`` / ``events_log.json`` under "
"``network_api/.Flow`` and cleared; ``close`` flushes both stores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Network_APIs/TCP_Client_APIs.rst:373
#: 6d52a0605748445694e0f4b1a6c52ea7
